“From the wilds of Nepal, a melanistic leopard, more commonly known as a black panther, stops in its tracks to eye the WEAPON 4K trail camera deployed by @sonamtac of the @redpandanetwork,” wrote Solaris Trail Cameras in an Instagram post sharing the video footage. “Melanistic animals are quite a rare sight, and capturing them on camera is even rarer, so we are stoked to revisit this incredible footage from the beautiful country of Nepal!”

[RELATED: Caught on Trail Cam: Rare Footage of a Wild Pallas’s Cat]

The footage (and the cat itself) is stunning. The video shows the leopard stop and look around, before gracefully walking offscreen.

Watch a black leopard on a trail cam in Nepal below (or see it here).

